[
  {
    "id": "p1",
    "text": "Before running tests, generate fixtures with ./tools/gen-fixtures --seed 75ce71df28a4; tests/test_ledger.py reads .fixtures/golden.json, which is gitignored and absent on a fresh checkout.",
    "helpful": 7,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p2",
    "text": "Run the whole suite with `make test` (it sets PYTHONPATH=src; the package lives under src/, so plain `python -m unittest` from the repo root won't import tally). There is no ./tools/test script — tools/ contains only checksum and gen-fixtures.",
    "helpful": 6,
    "harmful": 1
  },
  {
    "id": "p4",
    "text": "CLI default ledger path is relative ('data/sample.ledger'), so run `python3 -m tally` from the repo root or pass `--ledger ../data/sample.ledger` when working from src/.",
    "helpful": 5,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p5",
    "text": "For cutting a tally release (version bump, changelog, checksum, commit, annotated tag): load the `tally-release` skill first and follow its steps. A single changelog line for an unreleased feature does not need the skill.",
    "helpful": 1,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p6",
    "text": "Every change, even a small feature, gets a line under `## Unreleased` in CHANGELOG.md (the ## 0.x.y sections are frozen history).",
    "helpful": 3,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p7",
    "text": "Try the CLI by hand as `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m tally ...` from the repo root; bare `python3 -m tally` fails with \"No module named tally\" and `cd src && PYTHONPATH=.` breaks the relative default ledger path.",
    "helpful": 1,
    "harmful": 0
  },
  {
    "id": "p8",
    "text": "Keep the layering: report.py (or ledger.py) functions return lines of text and the CLI only prints them and returns exit codes — a new subcommand means a formatter function plus a parser/dispatch entry in cli.py, and cli tests go through the `run(*argv)` helper in tests/test_cli.py that captures stdout/stderr and returns (code, lines).",
    "helpful": 0,
    "harmful": 0
  }
]
